<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to draft economic plan by August.</title>
<headline>Hungary to draft economic plan by August.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary plans to work out a long-term economic programme by August, in preparation for membership talks with the European Union (EU), the Finance Ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We hope that we will complete the plan by the end of the summer,&quot; Deputy Secretary of State Tamas Tetenyi told a news conference.</p>
<p>The plan will include Hungary's economic forecast for the period until the country joins the EU, he said, adding that membership talks were likely to begin at around the end of 1997.</p>
<p>Hungary hopes to join the EU in the early 2000s.</p>
<p>-- Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
